# GitHub formats (Russian, impersonal)
- Commit title `<тип>(<сервис>): <что сделано>`; squash adds ` (#NN)`.
- Types: `разработка`, `исправление`, `тесты`, `аналитика`, `инфраструктура`, `зависимости`, `документация`.
- Services: `чат`, `каталог`, `бронирование`, `identity`, `медиа`, `шлюз`, `фронт`, `ci`, `деплой`, `бд`, `общее`, `процесс`; wiki `вики`.
- Body (non-trivial):
  ```
  Зачем: <какую проблему решает>
  Как работает: <коротко, что поменялось>
  Задача: #NN
  ```
- Examples:
  ```
  исправление(медиа): подпись тела файла при загрузке в MinIO по HTTP (#60)

  Зачем: на dev POST /media/upload отвечал 500 на любой файл.
  Как работает: DisablePayloadSigning включается только для https, по http тело подписывается.
  Задача: #59
  ```
  ```
  разработка(каталог): публичная выдача туров (#61)
  ```
  ```
  инфраструктура(ci): проверка PR без деплоя, actions закреплены по SHA
  ```
  ```
  зависимости(фронт): обновить vitest и tinypool
  ```
- Dependabot `commit-message.prefix` per ecosystem (Dependabot appends the bump text after the prefix; no `include: scope`): nuget `зависимости(общее)`, npm `зависимости(фронт)`, docker `зависимости(деплой)`, github-actions `зависимости(ci)` (see `.github/dependabot.yml`).
- PR title = commit title without number. Sections: «Что сделано», «Зачем», «Как это работает» (simple example first), «Как проверить», «Задача» (`#NN` only, or «без задачи» for rare docs/process-only meta PRs with no tracker task). Never «Учебный кейс» in PR/commits/issues (learning notes go only to the owner chat). Never use GitHub `closes`/`fix`/`fixes` in the PR body or commits before acceptance: merge must not auto-close the issue. Name the `Doc-` page updated or «вики не затронута». Impersonal Russian («убрано», not «убрал»): no personal names, no role labels as people, no agent or role as the actor, no «я/мы сделали», no `Co-authored-by` for bots. When clarity needs it, name Cursor Automations. Tick template checkboxes that hold.
- **Issue ↔ branch during work; closedBy only after close (unless Dependabot):** (1) branch `type/NN-short-english-slug` (ASCII lowercase English only; see `playbook-git-pr.mdc` «Branch naming»), created with `gh issue develop <NN> --name type/NN-short-english-slug --base main` so `linkedBranches` records the link (`gh issue develop --list <NN>`); (2) PR `## Задача` is `#NN` only, never `closes`/`fix`/`fixes`; (3) do not call `addCloseIssueReferences` and do not attach a closedBy / Development PR chip before acceptance. If the branch already exists, do not add or remove Development links by hand. The close workflow matches a merged PR when the issue number is its own branch segment and/or the PR title or body contains `#NN` (a closing keyword is not required). (4) Before merge, confirm that match is possible (linked branch or branch segment, plus `#NN` in «Задача»). Missing `#NN` on a tracked task is a process bug to fix in the PR text. Do not "fix" it with `addCloseIssueReferences`. Dependabot: no issue link. Docs-only meta with no tracker task: «без задачи». Do not retrofit old closed issues. (5) After acceptance on dev (+ Doc- if needed): set `статус: готово`, then close the issue. A follow-up comment may note the merged PR. Workflow `.github/workflows/link-closed-by.yml` sets the Projects PR chip. Agents do not add or remove Development links after close. Carve-out for any manual Development add/remove: the owner explicitly asks.
- Comments (do not casually rewrite published ones; delete+repost only to remove a forbidden leak such as a personal name, a role label used as a person, a retired chat-bot name, or a secret). Short copy-paste: `.cursor/templates/issue-comment.md`. Full rule stays here:
  ```markdown
  **Итог:** одна фраза
  **Подробно:** факты, sha, шаги, без секретов
  **Дальше:** следующий шаг или «нет»
  ```
- Issue: title as commit; body «Зачем», «Что сделать», «Критерии приёмки» (testable), «Связи» (epic, issues, PR, wiki page). Epic adds sub-issues. In issue/PR comments: no personal names, no role labels as people, no agent or role as the actor, no «я/мы сделали». When clarity needs it, name Cursor Automations. Otherwise write «взято в разработку», «ветка `…`», «PR #NN».
## Board statuses
- **Status labels always:** every issue has exactly one of `статус: очередь|в работе|на ревью|готово|удержание`. On create → `статус: очередь` plus a type label (`bug` / `enhancement` / `documentation` / `question`, or `тип: родительская` / `тип: бэклог`). On take → `статус: в работе`. On owner-decision wait → `статус: на ревью`. After acceptance (or not planned), at close time → set `статус: готово` and close the issue in the same moment. Never leave closed issues with any other status label. Label `статус: …` drives the column (`board-sync.yml`). Agents set the label only. They do not move Projects columns, set the project Status field, or edit view filters. `board-sync.yml` moves the card. Carve-out: the owner explicitly asks to move a card. Also `тип: бэклог`, `тип: родительская` (epic + field «Тип» = «Эпик»).
- Очередь: nobody on it. В работе: someone works on it (incl. review, test, deploy, Doc- after merge); set at once when taken. На ревью: ONLY when the owner must decide. Готово: only after acceptance on dev (and Doc- gap closed if required), or closed as not planned. Closing the GitHub issue moves the card to Готово (`board-sync`); therefore close the issue only at that moment, never from the PR body.
- Owner question: issue comment «**Итог:** требуется решение владельца» / «**Подробно:** вопрос, варианты, рекомендация» / «**Дальше:** после ответа задача вернётся в работу», set На ревью, tell the lead.
- Code review is not «На ревью»: the task stays В работе.
- Epic (`тип: родительская`): the moment any sub-issue becomes `статус: в работе` or `статус: готово` (or is closed), set the epic to `статус: в работе` and drop `статус: очередь` in the same edit. Keep В работе while some children are still open. When every child is Готово/closed, set the epic to `статус: на ревью` and run owner epic acceptance (`playbook-step-07-acceptance.mdc`); Готово (+ close) only after the owner accepts (or after gaps are filed and a later pass). На ревью also when the owner must decide on the epic itself for other reasons. Lead owns this sync on take/close of a child (board-sync does not infer epic status from children yet).
- Owner answer: the lead records it on the issue impersonally («**Итог:** решено: ...») and sets В работе (or Готово).
- Views: «Задачи» (all except epics, by field «Тип») and «Эпики» («Тип» = «Эпик»). Ordinary tasks: no «Тип».
- Card order: Очередь top = next (field «Приоритет», 1 = next, set by the lead; then bugs, then the rest, on-hold last); Готово newest first. `board-sync.yml` (`.github/scripts/board_order.py`, on issue events, daily, manual) syncs columns, **aligns status labels with issue open/closed state**, orders cards, adds missing issues, archives items closed 30+ days, clears «Приоритет» when a card leaves Очередь.
- Labels: the lead owns priorities, the architect keeps labels current; everyone sets the label on the task they take or finish.
- **Process gaps (holistic):** any process inconsistency (labels, commits, PR wording, statuses, docs, branch links, closedBy chips, board, wiki, open PRs) is a symptom that order, staged delivery, or throughput may be drifting. Fix the live artifacts and update these rules / playbooks in the same delivery cycle. A process change must be deliberate and complete: before shipping it, scan related rules, templates, automations, board-sync, and recent examples for side effects; update every place that would otherwise diverge. Do not ship a local patch that breaks consistency elsewhere.
